      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for Packers And Movers Ranchi To Pune</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you hire <strong>movers and packers Ranchi</strong> for a relocation to Pune, the move is governed by a set of statutory documents that protect both the client and the service provider. The first mandatory paper is the <strong>GST e‑Way Bill</strong>.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This electronic bill is generated on the GST portal for every consignment whose value exceeds ₹50,000 and it records the source (Ranchi), destination (Pune), and the declared value of goods.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The e‑Way Bill must travel with the cargo and be presented to any checkpoint or police officer during the journey, ensuring compliance with the Goods and Services Tax Act and preventing penalties.</span></li></ul>

<p>The second essential document is the <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR) or Bilty</strong>. Issued by the transporter, the LR serves as a proof of receipt, detailing the nature of goods, weight, packing condition, and the agreed‑upon freight charges.</p>
<p>It also records the signatures of the consignor (you) and the driver, establishing a clear chain of custody. For <em>Ranchi transport</em> services, an IBA‑approved LR is a legal safeguard that can be used in case of disputes or claims.</p>

